meta {
  name: Delete User (Truck Manager)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{truckManagerUserId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  truckManagerUserId: 22366
}

docs {
  Soft-deletes a user (`UserResource.deleteUser`, `common/controller/UserResource.java:351`,
  service `UserService.deleteUser`). Roles: VAHN_ADMIN, TORG_ADMIN, FUND_MANAGER,
  FUEL_STATION_MANAGER.
  
  For a TRUCK_MANAGER the service moves any wallet balance back to the admin wallet, unassigns
  the user from all their trucks, then marks the user deleted. OPERATOR and ACCOUNTANT users are
  only marked deleted. Any other role is rejected.
  
  Set `truckManagerUserId` (and `accessToken`) in the selected environment before each run.
  
  204 on success. 400 "User not found" if the id doesn't exist, "User is already deleted" on a
  repeat call, "Unsupported user role for deletion" for other roles, or "Failed to transfer
  balance to admin wallet, please try again later" if the wallet sweep fails.
  
  The service does not check that the target user belongs to the caller's torg (that check is
  commented out), so double-check the id before running.
}
​